1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:01,856
It's late.

2
00:00:01,876 --> 00:00:06,045
The rain has been talking to the window for almost an hour.

3
00:00:06,145 --> 00:00:09,224
Maya has been talking to no one at all.

4
00:00:09,324 --> 00:00:13,374
Then her grandfather, Abe, shuffles in with two cups of tea,

5
00:00:13,374 --> 00:00:17,904
because that is what he does when a light stays on too late.

6
00:00:18,004 --> 00:00:19,391
ABE: You're either studying,

7
00:00:19,411 --> 00:00:20,719
ABE: or you're hiding.

8
00:00:20,819 --> 00:00:22,450
MAYA: A little of both.

9
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:24,354
MAYA: Can I try something out loud?

10
00:00:24,374 --> 00:00:26,203
MAYA: It might sound strange.

11
00:00:26,303 --> 00:00:28,861
ABE: Strange is my favorite flavor.

12
00:00:28,961 --> 00:00:30,343
MAYA: It's a thought experiment.

13
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:33,258
MAYA: Every time the text says Christ, or Jesus,

14
00:00:33,278 --> 00:00:34,594
MAYA: I replace it with

15
00:00:34,614 --> 00:00:36,374
MAYA: the one reading this.

16
00:00:36,474 --> 00:00:37,908
ABE: Hm.

17
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:39,462
MAYA: Not to erase him.

18
00:00:39,482 --> 00:00:44,171
MAYA: I just want to see what happens when the words stop being about someone far away,

19
00:00:44,191 --> 00:00:47,311
MAYA: and start being about the person holding the page.

20
00:00:47,411 --> 00:00:48,914
ABE: Like holding up a mirror,

21
00:00:48,934 --> 00:00:50,632
ABE: instead of a window.

22
00:00:50,732 --> 00:00:51,699
MAYA: Yes.

23
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:53,275
MAYA: Exactly that.

24
00:00:53,375 --> 00:00:54,326
ABE: Alright then.

25
00:00:54,346 --> 00:00:56,024
ABE: Read me one.

26
00:00:56,124 --> 00:00:58,265
MAYA: The shortest verse in the whole book.

27
00:00:58,285 --> 00:00:59,818
MAYA: Jesus wept.

28
00:00:59,918 --> 00:01:00,756
MAYA: So.

29
00:01:00,776 --> 00:01:02,313
MAYA: The one reading this

30
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:03,675
MAYA: wept.

31
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,813
ABE: That one doesn't need any help, does it.

32
00:01:06,913 --> 00:01:07,688
MAYA: I did.

33
00:01:07,708 --> 00:01:08,987
MAYA: On Wednesday.

34
00:01:09,007 --> 00:01:11,312
MAYA: In the car, in the parking lot at work.

35
00:01:11,332 --> 00:01:13,721
MAYA: I thought it meant I was weak.

36
00:01:13,851 --> 00:01:14,971
ABE: Turns out

37
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:16,714
ABE: it's scripture.

38
00:01:16,814 --> 00:01:18,975
Something in the room shifts.

39
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:22,911
The words are no longer a statue on a high shelf.

40
00:01:22,931 --> 00:01:25,522
They are sitting at the table.

41
00:01:25,622 --> 00:01:27,238
MAYA: Mark, chapter ten.

42
00:01:27,258 --> 00:01:29,582
MAYA: A rich young man walks away from him,

43
00:01:29,602 --> 00:01:30,842
MAYA: and it says,

44
00:01:30,862 --> 00:01:33,571
MAYA: Jesus, looking at him, loved him.

45
00:01:33,671 --> 00:01:35,116
MAYA: The one reading this,

46
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:36,312
MAYA: looking at him,

47
00:01:36,332 --> 00:01:37,670
MAYA: loved him.

48
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:39,643
ABE: And what does that one ask of you?

49
00:01:39,743 --> 00:01:42,139
MAYA: To look at people long enough to love them.

50
00:01:42,159 --> 00:01:44,274
MAYA: Even the ones who walk away.

51
00:01:44,374 --> 00:01:46,305
ABE: Especially those.

52
00:01:46,405 --> 00:01:49,684
He glances at the photograph by the door.

53
00:01:49,704 --> 00:01:51,476
He doesn't explain.

54
00:01:51,496 --> 00:01:53,704
She doesn't ask.

55
00:01:53,934 --> 00:01:54,872
MAYA: Here's another.

56
00:01:54,892 --> 00:01:57,903
MAYA: When Jesus saw the crowds, he was moved with compassion,

57
00:01:57,903 --> 00:02:00,346
MAYA: because they were weary and scattered,

58
00:02:00,366 --> 00:02:02,210
MAYA: like sheep without a shepherd.

59
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:04,522
MAYA: When the one reading this saw the crowds,

60
00:02:04,542 --> 00:02:06,610
MAYA: they were moved with compassion.

61
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:07,377
ABE: So.

62
00:02:07,397 --> 00:02:09,410
ABE: That's you on the bus every morning.

63
00:02:09,510 --> 00:02:11,392
MAYA: That's everyone on the bus.

64
00:02:11,492 --> 00:02:13,228
ABE: Exactly.

65
00:02:13,358 --> 00:02:14,768
ABE: Try the hard one.

66
00:02:14,788 --> 00:02:16,384
ABE: The cross.

67
00:02:16,484 --> 00:02:18,299
MAYA: Then the one reading this said,

68
00:02:18,319 --> 00:02:19,983
MAYA: Father, forgive them.

69
00:02:20,003 --> 00:02:22,435
MAYA: They don't know what they are doing.

70
00:02:22,665 --> 00:02:24,600
MAYA: I can't say that one yet.

71
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:27,425
MAYA: There's someone I'm not ready to forgive.

72
00:02:27,855 --> 00:02:29,916
ABE: Then don't say it yet.

73
00:02:30,146 --> 00:02:32,021
ABE: Just notice that it's possible.

74
00:02:32,041 --> 00:02:33,393
ABE: That a human mouth,

75
00:02:33,413 --> 00:02:34,846
ABE: in that much pain,

76
00:02:34,866 --> 00:02:36,493
ABE: could make that sound.

77
00:02:36,593 --> 00:02:38,960
She doesn't let go of the stone.

78
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:41,483
But for the first time in months,

79
00:02:41,503 --> 00:02:44,480
her hand loosens around it.

80
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,733
MAYA: This one feels arrogant.

81
00:02:46,753 --> 00:02:49,245
MAYA: Jesus said, I am the light of the world.

82
00:02:49,345 --> 00:02:52,343
MAYA: The one reading this said, I am the light of the world?

83
00:02:52,363 --> 00:02:54,010
MAYA: I would never say that.

84
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:55,485
ABE: You don't have to.

85
00:02:55,505 --> 00:02:56,863
ABE: Look at Matthew five.

86
00:02:56,883 --> 00:02:58,723
ABE: He said it to them first.

87
00:02:58,743 --> 00:03:00,724
ABE: You are the light of the world.

88
00:03:00,824 --> 00:03:03,163
ABE: He was already running your experiment.

89
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:05,396
ABE: Handing the light across the table.

90
00:03:05,496 --> 00:03:06,748
MAYA: And telling them

91
00:03:06,768 --> 00:03:09,319
MAYA: not to hide it under a basket.

92
00:03:09,549 --> 00:03:10,694
MAYA: Philippians.

93
00:03:10,714 --> 00:03:12,221
MAYA: He emptied himself,

94
00:03:12,241 --> 00:03:14,109
MAYA: taking the form of a servant.

95
00:03:14,209 --> 00:03:15,580
MAYA: The one reading this

96
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,140
MAYA: emptied themselves,

97
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,224
MAYA: and took the form of a servant.

98
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:22,742
ABE: And then he knelt down with a towel, and washed their feet.

99
00:03:22,762 --> 00:03:24,498
ABE: Dusty, cracked feet.

100
00:03:24,518 --> 00:03:27,372
ABE: Even the feet of the friend who would betray him.

101
00:03:27,472 --> 00:03:29,369
MAYA: So the power isn't in winning.

102
00:03:29,469 --> 00:03:30,170
ABE: No.

103
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:31,972
ABE: The power is in kneeling,

104
00:03:31,992 --> 00:03:34,331
ABE: and refusing to strike back.

105
00:03:34,431 --> 00:03:36,756
MAYA: Some weeks I feel like that psalm.

106
00:03:36,776 --> 00:03:38,762
MAYA: Poured out like water.

107
00:03:38,862 --> 00:03:39,924
ABE: Poured out

108
00:03:39,944 --> 00:03:41,674
ABE: isn't the same as wasted.

109
00:03:41,774 --> 00:03:43,698
Where the water lands,

110
00:03:43,718 --> 00:03:46,900
something green decides to grow.

111
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:48,366
MAYA: And this one.

112
00:03:48,386 --> 00:03:50,064
MAYA: The one reading this said,

113
00:03:50,084 --> 00:03:52,298
MAYA: come to me, all you who are weary,

114
00:03:52,318 --> 00:03:54,278
MAYA: and I will give you rest.

115
00:03:54,378 --> 00:03:55,913
MAYA: That terrifies me.

116
00:03:55,933 --> 00:03:58,250
MAYA: I can barely carry myself.

117
00:03:58,350 --> 00:04:00,828
ABE: Nobody's asking you to carry anyone.

118
00:04:00,848 --> 00:04:04,041
ABE: Just to be a place where someone can set things down.

119
00:04:04,141 --> 00:04:05,609
ABE: Like a kitchen table,

120
00:04:05,629 --> 00:04:06,691
ABE: at midnight.

121
00:04:06,791 --> 00:04:07,714
MAYA: With tea.

122
00:04:07,814 --> 00:04:09,713
ABE: Always with tea.

123
00:04:09,943 --> 00:04:11,089
MAYA: Grandpa.

124
00:04:11,109 --> 00:04:12,458
MAYA: Is this wrong?

125
00:04:12,478 --> 00:04:15,178
MAYA: Am I making myself into God?

126
00:04:15,408 --> 00:04:16,911
ABE: If it made you proud,

127
00:04:16,931 --> 00:04:18,234
ABE: I'd worry.

128
00:04:18,334 --> 00:04:19,954
ABE: But look what it's done tonight.

129
00:04:19,974 --> 00:04:21,221
ABE: It made you weep.

130
00:04:21,241 --> 00:04:22,790
ABE: It made you look longer.

131
00:04:22,810 --> 00:04:24,464
ABE: It loosened your hand.

132
00:04:24,484 --> 00:04:26,976
ABE: It put you on your knees with a towel.

133
00:04:27,076 --> 00:04:28,347
ABE: That's not a crown.

134
00:04:28,367 --> 00:04:29,917
ABE: That's an apron.

135
00:04:30,017 --> 00:04:32,913
ABE: Some will say these words belong to him alone.

136
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:35,330
ABE: Others say he meant them to live in us.

137
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:36,505
ABE: Paul wrote,

138
00:04:36,525 --> 00:04:40,150
ABE: it is no longer I who live, but Christ lives in me.

139
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,152
MAYA: So maybe my experiment

140
00:04:42,172 --> 00:04:44,515
MAYA: is just reading that line slowly.

141
00:04:44,615 --> 00:04:48,255
ABE: Slowly is the only way I've ever understood anything.

142
00:04:48,485 --> 00:04:51,044
MAYA: Then here's the one I want to believe the most.

143
00:04:51,064 --> 00:04:53,082
MAYA: Neither death, nor life,

144
00:04:53,102 --> 00:04:55,161
MAYA: neither height, nor depth,

145
00:04:55,181 --> 00:04:59,931
MAYA: nothing in all creation can separate us from the love that is in Christ Jesus.

146
00:05:00,031 --> 00:05:01,144
MAYA: From the love

147
00:05:01,164 --> 00:05:02,238
MAYA: that is in

148
00:05:02,258 --> 00:05:04,201
MAYA: the one reading this.

149
00:05:04,431 --> 00:05:06,270
ABE: Then don't let one bad week

150
00:05:06,290 --> 00:05:08,119
ABE: argue you out of it.

151
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:10,549
ABE: One more, and then bed.

152
00:05:10,569 --> 00:05:11,282
ABE: He said,

153
00:05:11,302 --> 00:05:13,664
ABE: whatever you did for the least of these,

154
00:05:13,684 --> 00:05:15,227
ABE: you did for me.

155
00:05:15,327 --> 00:05:16,667
MAYA: Wait.

156
00:05:16,797 --> 00:05:19,312
MAYA: Then the experiment goes both ways.

157
00:05:19,332 --> 00:05:21,622
MAYA: He's already in the one reading this.

158
00:05:21,642 --> 00:05:23,243
MAYA: And the one reading this

159
00:05:23,263 --> 00:05:25,543
MAYA: is everyone I'll meet tomorrow.

160
00:05:25,643 --> 00:05:27,728
ABE: Now you're dangerous.

161
00:05:27,958 --> 00:05:29,707
The rain eases.

162
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:31,736
The tea has gone cold.

163
00:05:31,756 --> 00:05:34,277
Neither of them minds.

164
00:05:34,377 --> 00:05:35,263
MAYA: So.

165
00:05:35,283 --> 00:05:36,156
MAYA: You.

166
00:05:36,176 --> 00:05:37,324
MAYA: Yes, you.

167
00:05:37,344 --> 00:05:39,301
MAYA: The one reading this.

168
00:05:39,431 --> 00:05:41,790
If these words were about you,

169
00:05:41,810 --> 00:05:44,035
what would you do tomorrow?
